\textit{Yes. We use existing artifacts (pretrained models, evaluation framework).}

\begin{itemize}
\item[\checkmark] \textbf{B1.} Did you cite the creators of artifacts you used?

\textit{Yes. We cite the model zoo \citep{wang2025hybrid}, the evaluation framework \citep{gao2024lmeval}, and all individual architecture papers (GatedDeltaNet, RetNet, HGRN2).}

\item[\checkmark] \textbf{B2.} Did you discuss the license or terms for use and/or distribution of any artifacts?

\textit{The model zoo of \citet{wang2025hybrid} is publicly released. The lm-evaluation-harness \citep{gao2024lmeval} is open-source (MIT license). We do not release new artifacts.}

\item[\checkmark] \textbf{B3.} Did you discuss if your use of existing artifact(s) was consistent with their intended use?

\textit{Yes. The model zoo was designed for systematic comparison of hybrid architectures, which is exactly our use case. The evaluation harness was used with default prompts for standard benchmarks.}

\item[N/A] \textbf{B4.} Did you discuss the steps taken to check whether the data contains information that names or uniquely identifies individual people or offensive content?

\textit{Not applicable. We use established NLP benchmarks (LAMBADA, ARC-Easy, etc.) that have been widely used in prior work. No new data was collected.}

\item[N/A] \textbf{B5.} Did you provide documentation of the artifacts?

\textit{Not applicable. We do not release new artifacts.}

\item[N/A] \textbf{B6.} Did you discuss whether and how consent was obtained from people whose existing data you're using/curating?

\textit{Not applicable. All benchmarks used are established public datasets.}
\end{itemize}

\subsection*{C. Did you run computational experiments?}

\textit{Yes. We ran inference-only evaluation (no training).}

\begin{itemize}
\item[\checkmark] \textbf{C1.} Did you report the number of parameters in the models used, the total computational budget, and computing infrastructure?

\textit{Partially. We report model sizes (340M and 1.3B parameters) and the number of configurations evaluated (30 models $\times$ 10+ benchmarks). All evaluation was inference-only using the pretrained checkpoints of \citet{wang2025hybrid}; no model training was performed.}

\item[\checkmark] \textbf{C2.} Did you discuss the experimental setup, including hyperparameter search and best model selection?

\textit{Yes. \S3 describes the model zoo, task taxonomy, and all metrics. All models use default lm-evaluation-harness settings with no hyperparameter tuning or model selection.}

\item[\checkmark] \textbf{C3.} Did you report descriptive statistics about your results?

\textit{Yes. We report exact permutation tests, BCa bootstrap confidence intervals, Bonferroni and Benjamini--Hochberg corrections, effect sizes (Cohen's $d$, Jaccard similarity, normalized ES), and the ambiguity metric $\alpha$ of \citet{marx2020predictive}.}
\end{itemize}

\subsection*{D. Did you use human annotators?}

\textit{No.}

\begin{itemize}
\item[N/A] \textbf{D1--D5.} \textit{Not applicable. No human annotation was involved in this study.}
\end{itemize}

\subsection*{E. Did you use AI assistants?}

\begin{itemize}
\item[\checkmark] \textbf{E1.} Did you report the use of AI assistants?

\textit{Yes; see A4 above.}
\end{itemize}

